# Interface

Interfaces in Lince aspire to be as small as possible and as flexible as the
people using them need. The best interface may be almost interfaceless: Lince
should ask for as little attention as possible, make human choices quick, and
still leave every part under the person's control when they choose to engage
with it fully.

The brand is black and white by default, with purple as the supporting color.

Purple Cobalt — CMYK: 66, 71, 0, 36; HEX: `#3730A3`; RGB: 55, 48, 163.
Nocturnal Purple — CMYK: 59, 58, 0, 5; HEX: `#6366F1`; RGB: 99, 102, 241.
Deep Lead — CMYK: 10, 10, 0, 92; HEX: `#121214`; RGB: 18, 18, 20.
Gray — CMYK: 10, 5, 0, 12; HEX: `#A7B4C2`; RGB: 167, 180, 194.
Ice White — CMYK: 2, 1, 0, 1; HEX: `#F8FAFC`; RGB: 248, 250, 252.

Components are flat by default. A component may opt into the one restrained shadow utility when it needs to appear above an adjacent region; the area that is not content should feel tight and shrunk, boiled to the essence, minimal, functional.

